\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Associated Press and Reuters \par \uc2 533 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 November 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LABOR\par \par \uc2 Union Agrees to a Pause, Forestalling a Rail Strike\par \par \uc2 The possibility of an economically devastating railroad strike has been pushed back into early December to allow time for engineers and conductors to vote on their agreements with the freight railroads and give more opportunity for the industry to renegotiate with two unions that rejected their deals last month.\par \par \uc2 Previously, a Nov. 19 strike deadline hung over the talks, but the Brotherhood of Maintenance of Way Employes Division union that represents track maintenance workers agreed Wednesday to delay any action at least until Dec. 4. So for now, \uc2 BNSF\uc2 , Union Pacific, \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2 , \uc2 CSX\uc2 , \uc2 Kansas City Southern\uc2  and other railroads will continue to operate.\par \par \uc2 The railroads are offering the biggest raises workers have seen in more than four decades, but railroads have resisted demands to add paid sick time, and the new contracts won't resolve all the workers' quality-of-life concerns.\par \par \uc2 All 12 rail unions must approve their deals to prevent a strike. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 GAMBLING\par \par \uc2 Defying Inflation Worries, Casinos Have Big Quarter\par \par \uc2 Inflation? High gas prices? American gamblers are shrugging them off -- and losing money at casinos at a record pace.\par \par \uc2 Figures released Wednesday show the U.S. commercial casino industry had its best quarter ever, winning over $15 billion from gamblers in the third quarter.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American Gaming Association\uc2 , the trade organization for the casino industry, says the gambling halls are on track to have their best year ever in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Out of 33 states in which gambling was operational a year ago, 16 reported quarterly highs in overall gambling revenue, including five of the six largest markets: Indiana, Michigan, Nevada, New York and Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 ''Our sustained momentum in the face of broader economic volatility points to gaming's overall health today,'' said Bill Miller, the association's president.\par \par \uc2 David Schwartz, a gambling historian at the \uc2 University of Nevada Las Vegas\uc2 , said, ''I think it speaks to the continuing appeal of gambling, and that there may be even more appetite for it in uncertain times.'' ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 AUTOMOTIVE\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  Stock at 2-Year Low After Musk Sells Shares\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's shares slid to their lowest level in nearly two years on Wednesday after its chief executive, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , disclosed that he had sold another $3.95 billion worth of shares in the company.\par \par \uc2 Shares ended down 7.2 percent at $177.59, the lowest level since Nov. 23, 2020.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Musk's latest share sale fueled jitters about the fallout of his $44 billion acquisition of \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , analysts said. The acquisition sparked investor concerns, including whether Mr. Musk would be distracted from running \uc2 Tesla\uc2  or divert resources to the social media company.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  shares have fallen nearly 60 percent since touching a record high on Nov. 4 of last year. Four days after that, Musk started unloading his shares.\par \par \uc2 The latest sale brings the total amount of \uc2 Tesla\uc2  stock sold by Musk since last November to about $36 billion -- despite his having said earlier that he would sell no more of his shares. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPH BY WAYNE PARRY/ASSOCIATED PRESS) This article appeared in print on page B2. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020221110eiba0005i\par }\page {\par\