\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Eshe Nelson, Lauren Hirsch and The Associated Press \par \uc2 544 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 September 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RETAIL\par \par \uc2 Bed Bath & Beyond\uc2  Names\par \par \uc2 New C.F.O. After Suicide\par \par \uc2 Bed Bath & Beyond\uc2 , the beleaguered retailer, named Laura Crossen as interim chief financial officer on Tuesday, four days after the death of its former finance chief, \uc2 Gustavo Arnal\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Arnal, 52, died on Friday after a fall from a skyscraper that the New York medical examiner's office ruled a suicide. He was found near his residence, 56 Leonard Street, and ''appeared to suffer from injuries indicative from a fall from an elevated position,'' the \uc2 New York Police Department\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Arnal, who had been the company's chief financial officer since May 2020, was hired as part of an executive shake-up led by the chief executive at the time, \uc2 Mark Tritton\uc2 , who left in June.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Crossen, the retailer's chief accounting officer, has worked at \uc2 Bed Bath & Beyond\uc2  for more than 20 years and will also retain her current title. She most recently reported to Mr. Arnal.\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 Bed Bath & Beyond\uc2  fell more than 18 percent in trading on Tuesday. JORDYN HOLMAN and LAUREN HIRSCH\par \par \uc2 INTERNATIONAL\par \par \uc2 U.K. Leader's Relief Plan Gives Pound a Reprieve\par \par \uc2 The British pound inched away from its two-and-a-half-year low against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday after media reports that the new prime minister, \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 , would announce a major plan to freeze energy bills for households to ease the cost-of-living crisis.\par \par \uc2 The pound reached $1.16 amid reports that widespread relief was being considered, before reversing most of its gain and trading at about $1.15 by late afternoon in London. A cap on household electricity and gas bills is set to rise next month, with the average bill increasing 80 percent to 3,549 pounds, from about \u163\'00\'A32,000, or $2,317.\par \par \uc2 The pound's small reversal comes amid a long downward trend: This year, it has dropped about 15 percent against the dollar as the country's economic outlook has worsened with rising prices restraining consumer spending, normally a key driver of economic growth.\par \par \uc2 Even as the pound pushed higher on Tuesday, there are questions about how Ms. Truss's government will pay for the energy relief. ESHE NELSON\par \par \uc2 LABOR\par \par \uc2 Lufthansa Pilots' Union Calls Off 2-Day Strike\par \par \uc2 A union representing pilots at \uc2 Lufthansa\uc2  on Tuesday called off a planned two-day strike after a last-minute agreement with Germany's biggest airline in a pay dispute.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Vereinigung Cockpit\uc2  union had announced plans for a walkout on Wednesday and Thursday, calling on the company to make a ''serious'' offer in talks over pay increases. It would have been the second strike in a week after pilots staged a walkout Friday that led to hundreds of flights being canceled.\par \par \uc2 In hastily convened talks on Tuesday, the union said that the two sides agreed in principle on ''an extensive package of monetary and structural issues'' whose details would be thrashed out in the coming days.\par \par \uc2 Vereinigung Cockpit\uc2  has called for a 5.5 percent raise for its members this year and an inflation-busting 8.2 percent increase in 2023. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPH BY DADO RUVIC/REUTERS) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220907ei970004z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
